From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Utkarsh Dalal <dalal.utkarsh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:55:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] FEXCore: keep guest loads whose value is unused

The dead-flag pass removes any node with no uses and no declared side
effects. A plain LoadMem has none declared, so a guest load that only
fed a flag calculation goes away with the flags: once `add [rsi+0x128],1`
overwrites every flag `cmp rax,[rdx]` produced, the compare is removed,
and then the load behind it.

HotSpot relies on that load faulting. C1's explicit null check is
`cmp rax,[reg]` with the flags dead; the access violation at that PC is
what the JVM turns into a NullPointerException. With the load gone the
null receiver reaches the next field load, which faults at a PC that is
not in the nmethod's null-check table, and the VM aborts with
EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION reading 0xc. Necesse (Temurin 17 x86-64)
dies this way 13 s after start in
necesse.engine.save.LoadData.getInt/getBoolean, an 8-byte method whose
inlined invokevirtual is guarded by exactly that probe; every hs_err
has the same registers (rdx = 0 from the interpreted caller,
rsi = 0x46e, the live profile counter) and the event log records
"Implicit null exception at <pc> to 0x0", the lookup that found no
continuation. C2 safepoint polls (`test rax,[poll]`) are the same shape.

Declare the guest load ops as having side effects so the pass keeps
them; LoadMemPair already is. Loads that are truly dead stay in the
block, which compiled x86 rarely produces except as a probe.

A stand-alone probe (static method calling a virtual on its argument,
null every 5000th call, -XX:TieredStopAtLevel=3) reproduces the abort
on the stock build and passes with the loads kept.
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json
index 880520077..99cd57273 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json
@@ -530,6 +530,7 @@
       },
 
       "SSA = LoadMem RegisterClass:$Class, OpSize:#Size, GPR:$Addr, GPR:$Offset, OpSize:$Align, MemOffsetType:$OffsetType, u8:$OffsetScale": {
+        "HasSideEffects": true,
         "Inline": ["", "Mem"],
         "DestSize": "Size"
       },
@@ -575,6 +576,7 @@
       },
 
       "SSA = LoadMemTSO RegisterClass:$Class, OpSize:#Size, GPR:$Addr, GPR:$Offset, OpSize:$Align, MemOffsetType:$OffsetType, u8:$OffsetScale": {
+        "HasSideEffects": true,
         "Desc": ["Does a x86 TSO compatible load from memory. Offset must be Invalid()."
                 ],
         "Inline": ["", "Memtso"],
@@ -590,6 +592,7 @@
       },
 
       "FPR = VLoadVectorMasked OpSize:#RegisterSize, OpSize:#ElementSize, FPR:$Mask, GPR:$Addr, GPR:$Offset, MemOffsetType:$OffsetType, u8:$OffsetScale": {
+        "HasSideEffects": true,
         "Desc": ["Does a masked load similar to VPMASKMOV/VMASKMOV where the upper bit of each element",
                  "determines whether or not that element will be loaded from memory"],
         "ImplicitFlagClobber": true,
@@ -605,6 +608,7 @@
         "ElementSize": "ElementSize"
       },
       "FPR = VLoadVectorGatherMasked OpSize:#RegisterSize, OpSize:#ElementSize, FPR:$Incoming, FPR:$Mask, GPR:$AddrBase, FPR:$VectorIndexLow, FPR:$VectorIndexHigh, OpSize:$VectorIndexElementSize, u8:$OffsetScale, u8:$DataElementOffsetStart, u8:$IndexElementOffsetStart, OpSize:$AddrSize, i1:$MaskAllOnes{false}": {
+        "HasSideEffects": true,
         "Desc": [
           "Does a masked load similar to VPGATHERD* where the upper bit of each element",
           "determines whether or not that element will be loaded from memory.",
@@ -620,6 +624,7 @@
         ]
       },
       "FPR = VLoadVectorGatherMaskedQPS OpSize:#RegisterSize, OpSize:#ElementSize, FPR:$Incoming, FPR:$MaskReg, GPR:$AddrBase, FPR:$VectorIndexLow, FPR:$VectorIndexHigh, u8:$OffsetScale, OpSize:$AddrSize, i1:$MaskAllOnes{false}": {
+        "HasSideEffects": true,
         "Desc": [
           "Does a masked load similar to VPGATHERQPS where the upper bit of each element",
           "determines whether or not that element will be loaded from memory.",
@@ -637,6 +642,7 @@
         ]
       },
       "FPR = VLoadVectorElement OpSize:#RegisterSize, OpSize:#ElementSize, FPR:$DstSrc, u8:$Index, GPR:$Addr": {
+        "HasSideEffects": true,
         "Desc": ["Does a memory load to a single element of a vector.",
                  "Leaves the rest of the vector's data intact.",
                  "Matches arm64 ld1 semantics"],
@@ -776,6 +782,7 @@
         ]
       },
       "FPR = VLoadNonTemporal OpSize:#RegisterSize, GPR:$Addr, i8:$Offset": {
+        "HasSideEffects": true,
         "Desc": ["Does a non-temporal memory load of a vector.",
                  "Matches arm64 SVE ldnt1b semantics.",
                  "Specifically weak-memory model ordered to match x86 non-temporal stores."
